{#
  The clock and the search box, on every page.

  Search reads one index for the whole site, so a note is as findable from a
  post as it is from the stream. What the results replace differs: on the
  stream it is the list of notes, everywhere else it is the page itself -
  quirky.js picks whichever of the two is on the page.

  Sticky only on the stream. See _sass/quirky/_stream.scss: everywhere else
  main carries a top margin that a sticky head would slide up through on the
  first scroll.
#}
<div class="stream-head">
    <div class="quirky-now">
        <span id="quirky-date"></span>
        <span id="quirky-time"></span>
    </div>

    <div id="search-container">
        <input type="text" id="search-input" placeholder="Search&hellip;" autocomplete="off"
               aria-label="Search notes" aria-controls="results-container">
    </div>
</div>
<ul id="results-container" aria-live="polite"></ul>
